      "paragraph_source": "Differentiate $`xy`$ as $`1\\cdot y+xy'`$. The derivative of $`y^2`$ is $`2yy'`$. Put terms containing $`y'`$ on one side, factor out $`y'`$, then substitute the point. A tangent of slope $`m`$ through $`(1,2)`$ has equation $`y-2=m(x-1)`$. [Return to P3](lesson.md#p3)\n",
